WINDOWED vs FULL TRANSCRIPT READ -- the cost of flags.py's read path

corpus: 10 transcripts >= 524288 bytes, largest first (60 smaller skipped, 0 duplicate copies of a session under another account root dropped)
window: the newest 40 logical assistant turns      reps: 5 (median reported)

Each row: one real transcript. FULL reads byte 0 to EOF and parses every line.
WINDOW tail-seeks to the newest 40 turns. RESUME reads from the cursor a polling
caller would have kept -- i.e. what it costs to notice those 40 turns arrived.

