GREW DURING MEASUREMENT -- 1 file(s): the session appended while the three
reads were running, so the window legitimately saw a turn the full read
never did. This is NOT a mismatch between the two code paths -- it is a
live session, and the agreement question has no answer on it. Reported
separately and excluded from the figures below, so a growth artefact can
never be mistaken for the defect blind mode 3 looks for.
   sess-d24c66c8  (2895741 -> 2897700 bytes while measuring)

RESUMED TRANSCRIPT, DISCLOSED RESIDUAL -- 1 file(s): these replay a
`message.id`, so collect_turns merges two occurrences into one turn and the
full read's tail is NOT the window's content. Expected, bounded, and
documented in read_window's own contract -- NOT the unexplained read-path
disagreement MISMATCH is reserved for. Excluded from the figures below so
neither label can absorb the other.
   sess-3ef66434  (1186 turns, 17247 lines)

WHERE A SAVING IS POSSIBLE AT ALL -- the 8 file(s) with MORE than 40 turns:
   WINDOW / FULL, bytes read    median 0.237   best 0.075   worst 0.387
   WINDOW / FULL, lines parsed  median 0.271   best 0.080   worst 0.414
   WINDOW / FULL, wall-clock    median 0.139   best 0.052   worst 0.270
   RESUME / FULL, bytes read    median 0.097   best 0.046   worst 0.161
   RESUME / FULL, wall-clock    median 0.097   best 0.034   worst 0.198

