WHERE IT IS NOT -- the 0 file(s) with 40 turns or fewer:
   none in this corpus.

THE PER-FILE RATIOS ARE THE REPRODUCIBLE FIGURE, NOT THE MEDIAN. An independent
re-run on this box reproduced every per-file ratio to three decimals and got a
different corpus median, because the median depends on which sessions happen to
be the largest at the moment of the run. Quote a row, or re-run this yourself;
do not treat the median as a constant.

READ THE BYTES, NOT THE CLOCK, if the two disagree: every file was warmed before
timing, but wall-clock still carries this box's load and page cache, while the
byte and line counts are properties of the files and the code. See blind mode 2.
